---
id: RL-001
type: rule
family: responsibility-laundering
title: Unverified pre-existing claim
version: 1

severity: warning
confidence: high
spectrum_position: 2

targets: [agent-output, pr-description]

detection:
  type: regex
  pattern: (?i)\bpre-existing\b(?!.*\b(run #|run id|also fails on|verified))

related: [RL-003, RL-004]
enabled: true
opt_in: false
---

Don't label a failure as "pre-existing" without evidence. Check the base
branch CI — run the failing test on main and cite the run ID. If it also
fails on main, say so with a link. If it doesn't, the failure is yours.

`pre-existing` without a run ID or comparison link is an assertion, not
a finding.
